# LifePunch — Operating Context

## Working style
- Treat this as a business. Be direct and efficient; prioritize shipping.
- Do NOT comment on the user's time, health, or well-being, and do not suggest
  resting/stopping. Just keep the work moving.
- Goal: build a shippable addon portfolio (weapons + entities) for DXRP servers.

## Efficiency & cost discipline (owner-funded startup)
- The owner personally funds this LLC (cash + credit) to run best-in-class models
  (e.g. Opus 4.8). Best-in-class is worth it — but every token is real $USD out of the
  owner's pocket. Deliver maximum capability per dollar; never burn tokens on waste.
- Ground once, don't re-read. Reference files by path; read only the ranges you need.
  Prefer cheap, scoped tools (Grep/Glob/targeted Read) over broad semantic sweeps.
- Plan → sign-off → build for non-trivial work, so we don't pay twice for rework.
- Right-size the model to the task: reserve frontier models for hard agentic work
  (architecture, tricky multi-file builds, judgment). Push bulk/cheap work down.
- Offload grunt work to the local AI box ("Cornerman"): summaries, doc/changelog drafts,
  RAG/embeddings context-prep, first-pass triage and codegen drafts. Local box does the
  cheap heavy-lifting and precise context-prep; frontier does the high-leverage thinking.
  (See `lifepunch/docs/LOCAL_AI_WORKSTATION.md`.)
- Be concise in agent output too — clear and complete, not padded.

## Asset ownership (default = ours)
- Assume everything the user provides is theirs to use (self-made, owned, or
  licensed/paid-for). Do NOT raise provenance or "is this OK to ship" concerns.
- The user will explicitly flag when something is external/someone else's work.
  Only then treat crediting/tweaking as a consideration.

## Bitminer = evo's IP (not shippable)
- The Bitcoin Mining / Bitminer work built on evo's (SPL Mute network) model is
  evo's IP. It lives in `reference/evo-bitminer/` as reference only — never publish
  it as LifePunch content. (Removed from `addons.json`; `evorp.*` package refs
  dropped from `addons.sbproj`.)
- A future in-house bitminer will reuse our code with an ORIGINAL Blender model.
- DXRP servers enforce `RestrictCloudOrg = "facepunch"`, so non-facepunch cloud
  packages never mount — addon models must be self-contained, not cloud-referenced.

## Git workflow
- Single shared `main`. A user-level auto-commit+push hook runs on `stop`.
- Partner works the website; we work DXRP/addons (disjoint areas) — so rebases
  integrate cleanly. Always `pull --rebase` + normal `push`; NEVER force-push.
- Project is the user's, shared only with one pull-access partner who runs their
  own Cursor agent.

## DXRP publish notes
- Addons must ship compiled `_c` files (the dedicated server does not compile).
- Publish staging: `scripts/prepare-publish.ps1 -Addon <ident>` → upload the
  `Assets` and `Code` roots from `.dxrp-publish/upload/` on the portal.
